# The shell fixes on gate review 1, watched on the world the rest of this folder uses.
# Abandonment and construction are not in here because platted.toml declares no decline clock and
# builds its whole city at boot; fixes/declining.drive covers those two on a world that does both.
#
# Run it from the repository root, against a RELEASE build in the directory Godot loads:
#
#   dotnet build src/Borough.Godot -c Release \
#     -p:OutputPath=$PWD/src/Borough.Godot/.godot/mono/temp/bin/Debug/
#   BOROUGH_RENDER_PROFILE=1 godot --path src/Borough.Godot -- \
#     --ruleset rulesets/platted.toml --citizens 40000 \
#     --drive plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes.drive > plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/run.log 2>&1
#
# `ui family-bodies on` prints one family_body line per placed body, so run.log says which Family,
# size and Tile each picked Building id is. The draw lists and the JSON state dumps are read for
# their numbers and are not kept; the render profile beside each draw list is.

1 speed 8

600 ui family-bodies on
600 roads on
600 tilt 40
600 turn right
600 hold look

# opus-F2: the same camera path and the same 400 m stop as compare.drive, so the visible draw calls
# in band-0400.tsv.profile.tsv are comparable with final/400.tsv.profile.tsv's 1,538. The switch
# shot is the same frame with the fade off, which is the behaviour the band cost was measured on.
# Each state is given four Ticks to finish its uploads; read `pending` in the profile.
601 focus 556 560 3000
602 focus 556 560 1000
603 focus 556 560 500
604 focus 556 560 400
608 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400.png
609 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400.tsv

610 ui far-fade off
614 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400-switch.png
615 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400-switch.tsv

616 ui far-fade on
640 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400-fade.png
641 draw plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/band-0400-fade.tsv

# sol-F1/opus-F1: a mid-rise and a tower picked at each side of the fade and in the ring. The
# caption carries the selected Building id; `ui read` carries the whole InformationMapTargets list,
# which has to name each Building once.
642 focus 560 515 300
642 click 560 515
643 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-0300.png
643 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-0300.json

644 focus 560 515 475
644 click 560 515
645 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-0475.png
645 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-0475.json

646 focus 560 515 1000
646 click 560 515
647 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-1000.png
647 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/midrise-1000.json

648 focus 592 528 300
648 click 592 528
649 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-0300.png
649 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-0300.json

650 focus 592 528 475
650 click 592 528
651 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-0475.png
651 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-0475.json

652 focus 592 528 1000
652 click 592 528
653 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-1000.png
653 ui read plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/tower-1000.json

# sol-F2: a Building wash in the ring. One override used to dress both sides of the fade and draw
# the near and the far body on top of each other; each side wears its own copy now.
#
# The first shot is the wash arriving on bodies already standing. The second re-places every body
# under the armed wash, because `ui family-bodies on` invalidates, so the pair also says whether
# the two routes to a dressed body agree.
654 focus 560 515 475
654 overlay rung
655 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/wash-ring-0475.png

656 ui family-bodies on
666 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/wash-ring-placed-0475.png

667 overlay off
668 shoot plans/evidence/far-bodies/fixes/wash-off-0475.png

669 quit
